filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-10-10: UnicodeConverter
hands wchar_t to ICU as UTF-32.

Measured (2026-10-10, emscripten 4.0.11, its ICU 68.2): u_strFromWCS fails
with U_ILLEGAL_ARGUMENT_ERROR on any letter outside ASCII in the "C" locale
(ICU does not take emscripten's wchar_t for UTF-32 and goes through the C
library's wcstombs), while u_strFromUTF32 converts the same text.
CUnicodeConverter::fromUnicode then fell back to each character's low byte:
a txt or csv written as UTF-8 came out with "Sehir" (capital S with cedilla,
U+015E) as "^ehir". Where wchar_t holds more than 16 bits, the four calls go
through u_strFromUTF32WithSub / u_strToUTF32WithSub instead (an invalid code
point becomes U+FFFD); a 16-bit wchar_t (Windows) keeps u_strFromWCS.

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

